              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The famous episode of *Only Fools and Horses* in which Del Boy falls through the bar is titled **\"Yuppy Love\"**. \n\nHere are the details of this iconic TV moment:\n* **Season & Episode:** Series 6, Episode 1\n* **Original Air Date:** January 8, 1989\n* **The Scene:** Seeking to adopt a \"yuppie\" lifestyle, Del Boy (David Jason) and Trigger (Roger Lloyd-Pack) visit a trendy London wine bar. Attempting to play it cool and impress two women across the room, Del tells Trigger to \"play it nice and cool, son, nice and cool...\" He leans back to rest his elbow on the bar, completely unaware that the bartender has just lifted the bar hatch to walk through. Del plunges straight through the open gap and crashes onto the floor. \n* **The Punchline:** What makes the scene legendary is Trigger's reaction\u2014or lack thereof. Trigger, who was looking the other way, turns back to find Del gone, looks around the room in absolute bewilderment, and has no idea his friend has just fallen through the floor. \n\nThis moment is regularly voted by the British public as the funniest scene in sitcom history.",
